    <InstallationRequirements />

    <!-- Key Applications -->
    <h2 id="key-applications">Key Applications</h2>

    <h3>Crude Oil / Tank-Bottoms Dewatering</h3>
    <p>
      The DMPX-042 handles crude-oil dewatering and tank-bottom BS&amp;W (basic sediment and water) reduction for oil-field gathering stations, tank farms, and upstream production facilities. Crude-oil flow is application-specific; the published diesel and HFO values are not relabeled as crude-oil capacities.
    </p>

    <h3>Large-Scale HFO Purification</h3>
    <p>
      For large marine vessels, shore-power plants, and industrial boiler systems burning <a href="/fuel-oil-centrifuge/">heavy fuel oil</a>, published HFO 380 cSt capacity is 3,300 L/h (14.53 US GPM derived) for WHPX 409 and 4,200 L/h (18.49 US GPM derived) for WHPX 510, with viscosity specified at 50&deg;C and centrifugation at 98&deg;C. These are not MOPX ratings.
    </p>

    <h3>Industrial Waste Oil Processing</h3>
    <p>
      The DMPX-042 services large <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">waste oil</a> reclamation operations at fleet facilities, industrial plants, and centralized collection centers. Waste-oil throughput must be sized from the actual fluid properties and separation target. <a href="/explosion-proof-centrifuge/">Explosion-proof</a> options are available for hazardous locations.
    </p>

    <h3>Transformer Oil Purification</h3>
    <p>
      The DMPX-042 is used by utilities and industrial facilities to purify transformer oil in service, removing particulate contamination and free water. Transformer oil is not automatically assigned the OEM engine-lube or cross-head-lube capacities; Dolphin confirms flow from the actual viscosity, temperature, and separation target.
    </p>

    <h3>WVO, Yellow Grease &amp; Aluminum Drawing Oil</h3>
    <p>
      The DMPX-042 platform is used for <a href="/wvo-centrifuge-separator/">waste vegetable oil</a>, <a href="/yellow-grease-purification-centrifuge/">yellow grease</a>, and aluminum <a href="/cutting-oil-centrifuge/">drawing oil</a> duties. These application flows are sized separately and are not OEM diesel or HFO facts.
    </p>

