    <!-- DMPX Series Comparison -->
    <h2 id="dmpx-series-comparison">Where the DMPX-042 Fits in the DMPX Series</h2>
    <p>
      The DMPX-042 is the second-largest model in the Dolphin DMPX range. For medium industrial applications, the
      <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-028/">DMPX-028</a>
      is the step below. For compact or portable use, the
      <a href="/dmpx-014-self-cleaning-3-phase-disc-stack-centrifuge/">DMPX-014</a>
      and
      <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-010/">DMPX-010</a>
      serve smaller-scale needs. For the highest-volume industrial and power-generation applications, the
      <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-070/">DMPX-070</a>
      is the flagship class. All DMPX classes use automatic self-cleaning bowl technology, but capacities are compared only for exact base machines and fluids.
      See the full comparison at our <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">disc stack centrifuge overview</a>, or <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">contact us</a> for a sizing consultation.
    </p>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <h2 id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What is the throughput of the DMPX-042 centrifuge?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        DMPX-042 is not one universal flow rating. Published diesel capacities are MOPX 209: 7,900 L/h (34.78 US GPM derived); MOPX 210: 9,400 L/h (41.39 US GPM); WHPX 409: 8,400 L/h (36.98 US GPM); and WHPX 510: 10,700 L/h (47.11 US GPM), all at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt. WHPX rated-reference values have unspecified source fluids and are not a 69 GPM class rating.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What industries use the DMPX-042?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The DMPX-042 is used in oil field operations for crude oil tank-bottom dewatering, large-scale <a href="/biodiesel-centrifuge/">biodiesel</a> production, HFO purification at power plants and industrial boiler facilities, transformer oil purification, and high-volume industrial <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">waste oil</a> reclamation at manufacturing plants and fleet operations.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">Is the DMPX-042 available in explosion-proof configuration?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Yes. The DMPX-042 is available in Class I Division 1 and Class I Division 2 <a href="/explosion-proof-centrifuge/">explosion-proof</a> configurations for use in hazardous locations including oil fields, refineries, chemical plants, and offshore platforms. <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Contact us</a> to discuss hazardous-area requirements.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">How large is the sludge bowl on the DMPX-042?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The DMPX-042 features a 1.64–1.66-gallon sludge bowl - significantly larger than the <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-028/">DMPX-028</a>'s 1.03-gallon bowl. This larger capacity reduces ejection frequency and supports continuous operation even with high-solids streams such as crude oil tank bottoms and heavily contaminated <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">waste oil</a>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">How does the DMPX-042 compare to the DMPX-028 and DMPX-070?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Compare the <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-028/">DMPX-028</a>, DMPX-042, and <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-070/">DMPX-070</a> by exact base machine and fluid. DMPX-042 diesel values run from 7,900 L/h for MOPX 209 to 10,700 L/h for WHPX 510; HFO values exist only for WHPX 409 and WHPX 510. Visit the <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">disc stack centrifuge overview</a> to compare.
      </p>
    </details>

